  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb, reflexive — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "Often used with \"de\": *escaparse de casa/de la cárcel* (\"to run away from home/escape from jail\").",
    "Past participle is regular: **escapado**.",
    "Imperativo afirmativo reflexive pronouns attach to the end with a written accent to preserve stress (escápate, escápese, escapémonos, escápense); imperativo negativo places them separately in front (no te escapes...).",
    "*Don Justo se escapó de casa para buscar a su perro.* (\"Don Justo ran away from home to look for his dog.\")",
    "*El preso se escapó durante la noche.* (\"The prisoner escaped during the night.\")",
    "Related: *escapar* (non-reflexive, \"to escape,\" used similarly but with slightly less personal emphasis), *la escapada* (escape/getaway, noun), *huir* (synonym, \"to flee\")."
  ],
